  "comments": "<p>In the post-war years, mainly 1948 and 1950, 5 and 10 Reichspfennig (Deutsches Reich, KM #100 / #101) still remaining in Austria were struck over due to a lack of round material. Very rare are overstamped 1 Pfg (KM #97). Details of the original coin often remain visible.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Uncirculated example&nbsp;</p><p><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/68573cc6ea2db.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/68573cc6ea2db.jpg\"></a></p><p>Proof strike&nbsp;</p><p><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/68573cdcc98e1.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/68573cdcc98e1.jpg\"></a></p><p>@gdch6ng</p>",
